problems.problem:
The cost comparison uses a deliberately per-meme LLM judge and leaves out cheap reading rivals. The judge prefill is the same forward pass as the neuron extraction, so break-even is about 0 memes by construction. The neurons' whole cost advantage is the roughly 0.2 s per meme of question tokens. Missing alternatives:
- a single-pass multi-meme judge: the 24-meme sheet as a cached prefix shared by all stories, then the story, then a teacher-forced answer sheet scored in one forward pass;
- batching;
- a small LLM judge (Qwen3-1.7B or 0.6B);
- an NLI or zero-shot cross-encoder classifier.
Neuron setup cost (full-unit background extraction, about 2 GB per model, and 1.8 MB per work of storage) is listed but not part of the per-story frontier.
